# Website responsive & adaptive

Every page and UI change in `aoo-static-gh` must work on phone, tablet, and desktop without the user asking.

## Always

1. Include `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">` on every HTML page.
2. Build mobile-first: base styles for small screens, then `@media` for larger breakpoints.
3. Use fluid sizing where it helps: `%`, `max-width`, `clamp()`, `svh`/`dvh` for full-height layouts — not fixed widths that break on small screens.
4. Nav, hero, and main content must reflow: stack or collapse on narrow viewports (e.g. hamburger / drawer), not overflow horizontally.
5. Touch targets at least ~44×44px for buttons and primary links on mobile.
6. Images and logos: `max-width: 100%`, sensible `height: auto` (or fixed height with `width: auto` for marks). Prefer `srcset`/`sizes` when shipping multiple resolutions.
7. Before finishing, mentally check **~375px**, **~768px**, and **~1280px** widths — no clipped text, no horizontal page scroll, no overlapping controls.

## Suggested breakpoints (match existing home nav when possible)

| Name | Min width |
|---|---|
| Phone | default (&lt; 834px) |
| Tablet / desktop | `min-width: 834px` |
| Wide (optional) | `min-width: 1024px` or `1200px` |

## Never

- Do not ship desktop-only layouts.
- Do not use fixed pixel widths for full-page containers that cause horizontal scrolling.
- Do not hide critical actions only behind hover (no hover on touch).
- Do not assume the user will remind you to make it responsive.
